  "notes": "{除湿|じょしつ} is essential vocabulary for Japan's humid climate.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {除湿|じょしつ}する: to dehumidify\n- {除湿|じょしつ}モード: dehumidification mode (on AC)\n- {除湿|じょしつ}{機|き}: dehumidifier\n- {除湿|じょしつ}{剤|ざい}: desiccant, moisture absorber\n\nCONTEXT:\nVery commonly used during {梅雨|つゆ} (rainy season) and summer in Japan. Most air conditioners have a {除湿|じょしつ} mode.",
